  "comments": [
    {"at":0,"placement":"line","text":"Builds the 9 sprites of fighter_frame of fighter X into its hidden buffer, then publishes the 9 pointers. It toggles draw_buffer (0/1 fighter 0, 2/3 fighter 1). Facing 1 uses the mirrored copy at $33e7. Callers: anim_step and the time-up code $15f6."},
    {"at":14,"placement":"line","text":"Normal copy: slot n gets part table n ($7ae0 + n*$48) at fighter_frame. Slots 0-2 are row 1, 3-5 row 2, 6-8 row 3, left to right."},
    {"at":36,"placement":"side","text":"Starts with the 9 pointers of this buffer"},
    {"at":47,"placement":"line","text":"Slot 0: part index from $7ae0. Index 0 = empty slot, pointer 0 (the blank sprite at $c000)."},
    {"at":59,"placement":"side","text":"Source page = $7f00[part] + shape_page_offset"},
    {"at":78,"placement":"side","text":"Copies 64 bytes"},
    {"at":88,"placement":"side","text":"Next 64-byte sprite in the buffer, also for an empty slot"},
    {"at":504,"placement":"line","text":"Copies the 9 new pointers to fighter_part_ptrs ($02+2n+X); the IRQ at line 0 reads them. Then it looks for fighter_frame in shape_row4_frames."},
    {"at":553,"placement":"side","text":"Not in the list: row4_ptr_* keep their old values"},
    {"at":559,"placement":"side","text":"Facing 1: entries 8-15"}
  ],
